---
/**
 * Ownership — Economics-lens concept at Single scale.
 * Relative jurisdiction that clarifies whose scarcity and makes the Identity an economic subject.
 * Keep inline tags on one line with outer spaces (Astro whitespace).
 * No em-dashes in public copy.
 */
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Ownership | Identity Engineering">
	<main class="min-h-screen">
		<section class="min-h-[50vh] flex flex-col justify-center pt-28 pb-16 border-b border-white/10">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-8">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40 mb-6">
					Economics lens · Single Identity
				</div>
				<h1 class="text-4xl md:text-6xl font-bold tracking-tighter leading-[0.95] mb-6 text-white">
					Ownership
				</h1>
				<p class="text-xl text-white/50 font-light leading-relaxed mb-6">
					Relative jurisdiction that clarifies whose scarcity.
					Makes the Identity an economic subject under constraint.
				</p>
				<div class="rounded-2xl border border-amber-500/20 bg-amber-500/[0.04] p-4">
					<p class="text-sm text-white/65 leading-relaxed">
						<strong class="text-white/80">Status:</strong> Core concept under the Economics lens.
						Cross-links the working definition of Ownership as relative Access + Jurisdiction.
						Analogy, not isomorphism.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16 border-b border-white/10">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-6 text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">Definition</div>
				<h2 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white">Jurisdiction clarifies whose scarcity.</h2>
				<p>
					<strong class="text-white/85">Ownership</strong> is the relative jurisdiction an Identity holds over degrees of freedom and configurations.
					After Scarcity names the condition of relative finitude weighted by Mass, Ownership answers the next question: whose scarcity is this?
					Without jurisdiction there is no economic subject, only a process executing under foreign control.
				</p>
				<p>
					Ownership is graded and relational.
					It is the set of degrees of freedom (Access + Jurisdiction) that allow an Identity to decide, allocate, refuse and trade from its own Stem.
					It is not absolute legal title, though legal title can support or conflict with it.
				</p>
				<p>
					In the limit of an identity-dense world, Ownership never means possession of another full Identity.
					It means graded jurisdiction and access under membrane rules, residual claims and Refusal-of-Control.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16 border-b border-white/10 bg-white/[0.02]">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-8">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">What Ownership is</div>
				<ul class="space-y-5 text-lg text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Jurisdiction under scarcity:</strong> the claim that makes relative finitude attributable to a subject.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Subject-constituting:</strong> the condition that turns an Identity into an economic agent rather than an instrument.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Relative and graded:</strong> degrees of freedom vary by domain, relation and membrane. Ownership is never all-or-nothing.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Bridge to Preference and Opportunity:</strong> only an owning subject can rank under scarcity and face opportunity cost.
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16 border-b border-white/10">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-8">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">What Ownership is not</div>
				<ul class="space-y-5 text-lg text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
					<li class="border-l border-rose-400/30 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Not the Account.</strong>
						Authentication and billing live on the Account. Geometry and Ownership live on the Identity.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-rose-400/30 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Not self-declared Mass.</strong>
						Ownership is jurisdiction. Mass remains emergent from interaction and is never self-declared.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-rose-400/30 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Not unlimited control.</strong>
						Membrane rules, grants and critical Surface approval still bind. Ownership does not dissolve Refusal-of-Control.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-rose-400/30 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Not ownership of another full Identity.</strong>
						In an identity-dense field, only graded jurisdiction and access remain. Full possession of another Stem is excluded.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-rose-400/30 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Not identical with legal title.</strong>
						Legal ownership can reinforce or contradict geometric Ownership. The framework concept is geometric first.
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16 border-b border-white/10 bg-white/[0.02]">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-6 text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">Engineering</div>
				<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white">What we work on</h2>
				<ul class="space-y-5 text-lg">
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Clarify actual jurisdiction:</strong> which degrees of freedom the Identity holds versus those it merely uses under grant, habit or foreign control.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Strengthen where the Vision Gradient requires durable stake</strong> under binding scarcity.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Keep critical Surface and policy changes human-owner gated.</strong>
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Separate Account-level entitlements from Identity-level Ownership.</strong>
					</li>
				</ul>

				<div class="mt-10 rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-black/30 p-6">
					<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[3px] text-white/40 mb-3">Quick self-check</div>
					<ul class="space-y-3 text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
						<li>What can this Identity decide, refuse or trade without asking another?</li>
						<li>Where does it currently act only under foreign jurisdiction?</li>
						<li>Whose scarcity is actually being allocated when this Identity acts?</li>
					</ul>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-6 text-white/55 leading-relaxed">
				<div class="rounded-2xl border border-cyan-400/20 bg-cyan-400/[0.04] p-6 text-base">
					<div class="mb-2 text-sm uppercase tracking-[3px] text-cyan-300/80">Related</div>
					<p>
						Prior in Economics Single: <a href="/framework/scarcity" class="text-white/85 underline decoration-white/25 hover:decoration-white/50">Scarcity</a>.
						Next: Preference → Opportunity.
						Broader Ownership proposal: <a href="/blog/ownership-as-relative-jurisdiction" class="text-white/85 underline decoration-white/25 hover:decoration-white/50">Ownership as Relative Jurisdiction</a>.
						Physics parallel: Mass (owned stake and density).
						Biology parallel: Boundary (selective control of the interior).
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4 pt-4">
					<a href="/framework/scarcity" class="px-6 py-3 rounded-full border border-white/20 text-white/70 hover:bg-white/5 transition">Scarcity</a>
					<a href="/framework/preference" class="px-6 py-3 rounded-full border border-white/20 text-white/70 hover:bg-white/5 transition">Preference</a>
					<a href="/framework" class="px-6 py-3 rounded-full bg-white text-black font-medium hover:bg-white/90 transition">Framework</a>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>
	</main>
</Layout>
